<title>USA: Weirton Steel in tentative pact with union.</title>
<headline>Weirton Steel in tentative pact with union.</headline>
<dateline>WEIRTON, W.Va. 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Weirton Steel Corp said Friday it has reached a 56-month tentative contract agreement with the Independent Guard Union.</p>
<p>It said details of the accord, affecting 42 security personnel, will not be made public until the union completes a review of the package with its members, it said.</p>
<p>The agreement is the final pact to be negotiated by the company and its four bargaining units, it said.</p>
<p>Earlier this year, Weirton Steel and the Independent Steelworkers Union settled on 54-month contract agreements with the union's three bargaining units which cover about 4,500 employees, it said.</p>
</text>
